/* A card surface inside an elevation wrapper - the arrangement Theme.uss's
 * header note 2 forces and the Primitives fixture demonstrates:
 *
 *     <ui:VisualElement class="elev-1">
 *         <ui:VisualElement class="card"> ... </ui:VisualElement>
 *     </ui:VisualElement>
 *
 * Here the OUTER element is the component root - it carries `section-card`
 * and `elev-1` - and the inner one is `section-card__surface`. The first
 * consumer of Task 3 in the app, after one task in which .elev-1 and .elev-2
 * had zero usages anywhere in client/.
 *
 * THIS FILE SETS NO PADDING ON THE ROOT, and that is not an omission.
 * `.elev-1` IS padding - var(--elev-1-spread), 6px - and that padding is
 * exactly where the nine-slice's falloff is drawn. A second padding
 * declaration on the same element at the same specificity would be decided
 * by stylesheet order, and whichever won would either swallow the shadow or
 * silently move the card edge off the slice scale the texture was cut for.
 */
.section-card {
    flex-direction: column;
    /* One step below Theme.uss's `.card` (12px), because the wrapper already
     * contributes 6px of its own below the surface and 6px above the next
     * one - so two stacked cards sit ~20px apart at their white edges, which
     * is the gap `.card` gives without a shadow.
     *
     * STILL TRUE AFTER TASK 9 GAVE `.elev-1` A NEGATIVE MARGIN, because that
     * margin is HORIZONTAL ONLY. Vertically the wrapper's padding is exactly
     * where the drop falls - measured between two of these cards, 6px of ink
     * reaching 4/255 below a surface against 2px at 1/255 above the next -
     * and cancelling it would put one card's white edge inside the other's
     * shadow and close this 20px to 8px. Theme.uss's elevation block carries
     * the full argument. Measured again after that change: 20px, unmoved. */
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}

.section-card__surface {
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: var(--space-4);
}

/* Layout only - the 19px Baloo 2 face and --ink come from `t-section`. */
.section-card__heading {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}

.section-card__body {
    flex-direction: column;
}
